 # PCA Rotation
 ## Overview
-PCA Rotation aligns a mesh so that its first principal axis aligns with the positive X-axis and its second principal axis aligns with the positive Y-axis [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of orienting geometry relative to its intrinsic shape distribution, which is a prerequisite for consistent voxelization or spatial hashing in volume rendering pipelines. It differs from [Rotation Alignment Matrix](2699-rotation-alignment-matrix.md) by deriving the rotation from the data's statistical covariance rather than rotating between two arbitrary vectors.
