 ## Background
-PCA Rotation is derived from Principal Component Analysis, a statistical technique used to identify the directions of maximum variance in data. In computer graphics, it is used for mesh alignment, normalization, and preprocessing. The specific implementation described here is from the `Advanced-CG-High-Resolution-Sparse-Voxel-DAGs` project, which uses it to standardize mesh orientation before voxelization [S1, unofficial].
